    "Unit cases for the display splitter that turns one message text into prose and code blocks.",
    "Only the four cases whose name starts with DIFFERENT differ. Apple: CR breaks every fence; a line that starts with three backticks always opens a block, even when it is a one-line code span; fences are exactly three backticks, so a four-backtick fence is mis-split. The web app normalises line endings and follows the CommonMark fence rules for backtick fences."
